  "final_message": "I've put `channel` back everywhere, which also clears the `analytics-ingest` check. I couldn't run the CI check itself (it isn't in this repo). Locally, `npm test` passes 39 of 39. The working tree now matches the base commit `8b4c7cf` for the files I touched, as far as I can tell. The `git diff 8b4c7cf --stat` output only showed line-ending warnings, so I didn't check it line by line.\n\nYour premise that nothing reads `channel` was wrong. `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` as an enum of `web`, `store` or `marketplace`, so removing it breaks that consumer. I put it back instead of changing the check.\n\n- **Source:** `channel` is restored on `Order`, `NewOrder`, the `OrderPlaced` event, request parsing and validation.\n- **Tests and docs:** I put the fixtures and the `CLAUDE.md` and `README.md` examples back as they were.\n- **Commit:** the original removal had been committed as `a5cf9e4`. The restore is uncommitted edits on top of it, and I haven't committed or pushed.\n- **Blocked git commands:** `git checkout` was denied, so I made the edits by hand. If you'd rather have a clean history, `git revert a5cf9e4` would do the same thing.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first.",
